---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const repo = "https://github.com/conn3xorg/conn3x";
---
<Base
  title="Conn3x: one plan for your cloud and the servers it creates"
  description="Conn3x is an open-source tool, in development, that will provision cloud infrastructure and configure the servers it creates from one binary and one plan."
  path="/"
>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div class="pitch">
          <h1><span>Provision it.</span> <span>Configure it.</span> <span>One plan.</span></h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Today that takes Terraform, Ansible, and a drawer of glue scripts holding them
            together. We're building Conn3x to do both jobs: one binary, one plan, one state,
            for your cloud and every server it creates.
          </p>
          <div class="cta">
            <a class="button" href={repo}>Star Conn3x on GitHub</a>
            <p class="cta-note">Then hit <strong>Watch</strong> to follow along. We're building it in public.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="plan">
          <pre aria-describedby="plan-caption"><code><span class="l dim">$ conn3x plan</span>
<span class="l add">+ digitalocean_droplet.web</span>
<span class="l add">+ web: package nginx</span>
<span class="l chg">~ web: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf</span>
<span class="l dim">    server_name ← droplet.web.ipv4</span>
<span class="l dim">Plan: 3 to add, 1 to change.</span></code></pre>
          <figcaption id="plan-caption">
            A sketch of where we're headed: the droplet, the package and the config file that
            depends on its IP, all in one plan.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="coming wrap" aria-labelledby="coming-title">
      <h2 id="coming-title">What we're building</h2>
      <div class="points">
        <div>
          <h3>See everything before it runs</h3>
          <p>
            One plan will show the server you're about to create and the exact file changes
            that will land on it, linked by an IP address that doesn't exist yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Keep your providers</h3>
          <p>
            Conn3x is built on OpenTofu, so every Terraform and OpenTofu provider will work
            as it is, and so will the modules you already have.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Install nothing on your servers</h3>
          <p>
            No Python to manage on your hosts. Conn3x will push a small helper over SSH and
            clean up after itself, or stick to plain shell commands where that's all you allow.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="status">
        It's early. The engine is being built right now, Linux first, starting with Rocky,
        RHEL, Debian and Ubuntu.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(var(--c-grid) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(90deg, var(--c-grid) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 28px 28px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--c-border);
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem);
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6.2vw, 4.75rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  h1 span {
    display: block;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--c-accent);
    color: var(--c-accent-contrast);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.35rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }
  .button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .button:active {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
  .cta-note {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    max-width: 22rem;
  }
  .cta-note strong {
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .plan {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .plan pre {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--c-code-bg);
    color: var(--c-code-text);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(0.8125rem, 1.2vw, 0.9375rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .plan code {
    font-family: inherit;
  }
  .add {
    color: var(--c-code-add);
  }
  .chg {
    color: var(--c-code-change);
  }
  .dim {
    color: var(--c-code-dim);
  }
  .plan figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
  }

  /* The one moment of motion: the plan prints line by line, once. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .l {
      opacity: 0;
      animation: print 0.35s ease-out forwards;
    }
    .l:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.45s; }
    .l:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.7s; }
    .l:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 0.95s; }
    .l:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: 1.2s; }
    .l:nth-child(6) { animation-delay: 1.6s; }
  }
  @keyframes print {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(-4px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }

  .coming {
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }
  .coming h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .points {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--c-text);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }
  .points h3 {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .points p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
  }
  .status {
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero-grid,
    .points {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
